L711: ### B.6 Proof of cite134†Lemma 1 L712: 
L713: To prove cite134†Lemma 1 , we require the following result.
L714: 
L715: ###### Lemma 11.
L716: 
L717: Under cite90†(A1) to cite91†(A4) , the expectile $\xi_{\nu}(\theta)$ is Lipschitz continuous with respect to the parameter vector $\theta$. Specifically, there exists a constant $L_{m}$ such that for any $\theta_{1},\theta_{2}\in\Theta$:
L718: 
L719:  | $$\|\xi_{\nu}(\theta_{1})-\xi_{\nu}(\theta_{2})\|_{2}\leq L_{m}\|\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\|_{2},$$  |
L720: 
L721: where $L_{m}=\frac{2F_{\max}\max(\nu,1-\nu)S}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$.
L722: ###### Proof.
L723: 
L724: Using cite129†Theorem 4 , the gradient of the expectile is given by:
L725: 
L726:  | $$\nabla_{\theta}\xi_{\nu}(\theta)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[l_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))G(\theta)]}{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[l^{\prime}_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))]}.$$  |  | (49)
L727: 
L728: We bound the norm of the expectile gradient as follows:
L729:  | $\displaystyle\|\nabla_{\theta}\xi_{\nu}(\theta)\|_{2}$  | $\displaystyle=\left\|\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[l_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))G(\theta)]}{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[l^{\prime}_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))]}\right\|_{2}$  |
L730:  |  | $\displaystyle\leq\frac{\left\|\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[l_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))G(\theta)]\right\|_{2}}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$  |
L731:  |  | $\displaystyle\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[|l_{\nu}(F-\xi_{\nu}(\theta))|\cdot\|G(\theta)\|_{2}]}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$  |  | $\displaystyle\begin{aligned} &\text{(by Jensen's inequality and}\\
L732: &\text{\quad Cauchy-Schwarz inequality)}\end{aligned}$  |
L733:  |  | $\displaystyle\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[2F_{\max}\cdot\max(\nu,1-\nu)\cdot\|G(\theta)\|_{2}]}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$  |  | (using cite97†(A2) )  |
L734:  |  | $\displaystyle\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[2F_{\max}\cdot\max(\nu,1-\nu)\cdot S]}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$  |  | (using cite91†(A4) )  |
L735:  |  | $\displaystyle=\frac{2F_{\max}\max(\nu,1-\nu)S}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}.$  |  | (50)
L736: With the bound on the gradient norm from (cite135†50 ), we apply the Mean Value Theorem to obtain the main result:
L737: 
L738:  | $$\|\xi_{\nu}(\theta_{1})-\xi_{\nu}(\theta_{2})\|_{2}\leq L_{m}\|\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\|_{2},$$  |
L739: 
L740: where $L_{m}=\frac{2F_{\max}\max(\nu,1-\nu)S}{\min(\nu,1-\nu)}$. ∎
